270-271-272	698,835,1746,1942 - 698,1548,742,1578	270. Flower, bud, and leaf of White Water-Lily. 271. Flower with the parts cut away, all but two petal-like stamens, one ordinary stamen, and the compound pistil. 272. Slice across the 11-celled pistil.	A full-blown White Water-Lily with many pointed petals, a closed bud at right and a broad round leaf behind (270); below left, the flower cut back to its pistil and a few stamens (271); beside it, a round slice of the pistil showing its cells (272).
273	171,1491,572,1908	Fruit of Nelumbo.	The top-shaped fruit of the Nelumbo, its broad flat top pitted with holes, each holding a seed, above a ribbed body narrowing to the stalk.
